WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:08.380
Let's pray together. Day 20, Romans chapter 12,

2
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:09.720
making a full surrender.

3
00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:15.130
Lord, I thank you for the beautiful metaphor in your

4
00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:15.910
word today

5
00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:18.920
that calls us to yield ourselves.

6
00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:23.360
Oh God, we are so good at standing up for ourselves.

7
00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:27.070
We are so good at resisting every other

8
00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:30.780
call. We're so programmed to believe that our

9
00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:34.440
freedom is dependent on our own grasping of our

10
00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:37.440
strength and our right to determine ourselves.

11
00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:40.320
But oh God, you call us to a different path.

12
00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:45.050
You call us not to grasping for our own way

13
00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:48.940
and our own will, but yielding our own way and our own

14
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:49.220
will.

15
00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:54.180
And so, Lord, thank you. Thank you for teaching us that it's necessary

16
00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:58.180
for us to present our bodies. Thank you, Lord, for calling

17
00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:02.060
to us and reminding us of the importance of

18
00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:05.820
yielding it as Christians, holy and acceptable to God.

19
00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:10.240
So Lord, we do that right now. Here's our hands, Lord. Here's my hands.

20
00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:14.740
Take my hands and what I click and what I type and what I touch

21
00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:17.900
and what I do and how I work. Lord, here's my

22
00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:20.800
mind and my brain and what I think about and

23
00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:25.540
what I mull over and meditate on. Here's my mouth and what I take

24
00:01:25.660 --> 00:01:29.520
in and what I say and what I put out. Lord, here's my

25
00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:31.980
feet and where I go and where I stop.

26
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:35.840
And Lord, here's every part of me, my eyes and what

27
00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:38.900
I look at and the way I see people. Lord,

28
00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:42.940
here's my ears and what I listen to and what

29
00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:45.880
I hear. Lord, we yield ourselves

30
00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:49.460
wholeheartedly, body, soul, and spirit,

31
00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:53.580
everything given over to you. Not so

32
00:01:53.620 --> 00:01:57.060
that we will stop sinning, but because we've been made

33
00:01:57.120 --> 00:02:00.980
holy. Not because we're lost and broken, but because we've been

34
00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:04.920
made holy by the blood of Christ. We yield all these things because of

35
00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:08.440
your great mercy, because it just makes sense.

36
00:02:08.521 --> 00:02:12.400
It's the rational, reasonable, normal thing to do.

37
00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:14.920
So we surrender to you in Christ's name.

38
00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:19.640
You're probably hearing some noise in the background.

39
00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:23.480
As I told you a couple of days ago, I'm praying over each of you

40
00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:26.980
today as we seek the Lord together. I'm driving.

41
00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:30.600
I'm on my way to the hospital, and I'm just leaving the hospital from visiting

42
00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:34.320
someone. So thank you for putting up with the noises in the

43
00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:38.080
background. Let's continue seeking the Lord together now as we pray.
